<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
        <title>Exploring the Stanford Torus - Claire Nyquist</title>
        <meta
            name="description"
            content="Interactive 3D visualization of a Stanford Torus space habitat. Adjust radius, rotation, gravity, and more. Based on NASA SP-413 (1975)."
        />
        <meta property="og:title" content="Exploring the Stanford Torus" />
        <meta
            property="og:description"
            content="Interactive 3D visualization of a Stanford Torus space habitat based on NASA SP-413. Adjust parameters and explore the physics of artificial gravity."
        />
        <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
        <meta
            property="og:url"
            content="https://clairenyquist.com/stanford-torus-explorer"
        />
        <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
        <meta name="author" content="Claire Nyquist" />
        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
        <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
        <link
            href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400&display=swap"
            rel="stylesheet"
        />
    </head>
    <body>
        <canvas id="c"></canvas>
        <a id="back-link" href="/">&larr; clairenyquist.com</a>
        <div id="ui-title">
            <h1>EXPLORING THE STANFORD TORUS</h1>
            <p>
                NASA SP-413 &middot; Earth-Moon L5 Lagrange Point &middot;
                384,400 km from Earth &amp; Moon
            </p>
        </div>
        <div id="ui-stats"></div>
        <div id="ui-hint">
            Drag to orbit &middot; Scroll to zoom &middot; P to toggle
            parameters
        </div>

        <button id="panel-toggle" title="Toggle parameters (P)">
            <span class="label-full">EDIT TORUS SPECIFICATIONS</span>
            <span class="label-short">EDIT SPECS</span>
        </button>
        <div id="param-panel">
            <p id="panel-intro">
                This experimental visualization explores new artforms with AI.
                Core specifications are drawn from NASA SP-413 (1975), but
                parameter extrapolations&mdash;population estimates,
                habitability commentary&mdash;are speculative. See citations for
                primary sources.
            </p>
            <div class="panel-header">STATION PARAMETERS</div>
            <div id="torus-info"></div>
            <div class="param-row">
                <div class="param-label">
                    <span>Major Radius</span><span class="val" id="v-R"
                        >830 m</span
                    >
                </div>
                <input
                    type="range"
                    id="p-R"
                    min="200"
                    max="2000"
                    value="830"
                    step="10"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="param-row">
                <div class="param-label">
                    <span>Tube Radius</span><span class="val" id="v-r"
                        >65 m</span
                    >
                </div>
                <input
                    type="range"
                    id="p-r"
                    min="10"
                    max="200"
                    value="65"
                    step="5"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="param-row">
                <div class="param-label">
                    <span>Spokes</span><span class="val" id="v-spokes">6</span>
                </div>
                <input
                    type="range"
                    id="p-spokes"
                    min="2"
                    max="12"
                    value="6"
                    step="1"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="param-row">
                <div class="param-label">
                    <span>Rotation</span><span class="val" id="v-rpm"
                        >1.0 RPM</span
                    >
                </div>
                <input
                    type="range"
                    id="p-rpm"
                    min="0.1"
                    max="3.0"
                    value="1.0"
                    step="0.1"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="param-row">
                <div class="param-label">
                    <span>Mirror Tilt</span><span class="val" id="v-tilt"
                        >45&deg;</span
                    >
                </div>
                <input
                    type="range"
                    id="p-tilt"
                    min="10"
                    max="80"
                    value="45"
                    step="1"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="computed-stats">
                <div class="stat-row">
                    <span class="stat-label">Diameter</span><span id="c-diam"
                        >1,790 m</span
                    >
                </div>
                <div class="stat-row">
                    <span class="stat-label">Gravity (outer rim)</span><span
                        id="c-grav">1.00 g</span
                    >
                </div>
                <div class="stat-row">
                    <span class="stat-label">Rim Speed</span><span id="c-speed"
                        >93.7 m/s</span
                    >
                </div>
            </div>
            <button id="reset-btn">RESET TO STANDARD</button>
        </div>

        <button id="cite-btn">CITATIONS</button>
        <div id="cite-modal" class="hidden">
            <div class="cite-inner">
                <div class="cite-header">
                    <span>REFERENCES</span>
                    <button id="cite-close">&times;</button>
                </div>
                <div class="cite-body">
                    <h3>Primary Sources</h3>
                    <ol>
                        <li>
                            <strong>NASA SP-413</strong>: <em
                                >Space Settlements: A Design Study</em
                            > (1977). Richard D. Johnson &amp; Charles Holbrow, eds.
                            The foundational document for the Stanford Torus design.
                            <a
                                href="https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19770014162"
                                target="_blank">NASA NTRS</a
                            > &middot; <a
                                href="https://nss.org/settlement/nasa/75SummerStudy/index.html"
                                target="_blank">NSS Full Text</a
                            >
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Gerard K. O&rsquo;Neill</strong>: <em
                                >The High Frontier: Human Colonies in Space</em
                            > (1976). William Morrow &amp; Co.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Gerard K. O&rsquo;Neill</strong>: &ldquo;The
                            Colonization of Space,&rdquo; <em>Physics Today</em> 27(9),
                            September 1974, pp. 32&ndash;40.
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                    <h3>Life Support &amp; Agriculture</h3>
                    <ol start="4">
                        <li>
                            <strong>Silverstone et al.</strong>: &ldquo;Food
                            production and nutrition in Biosphere 2,&rdquo; <em
                                >Ecological Engineering</em
                            > 13 (1999). <a
                                href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11538814/"
                                target="_blank">PubMed</a
                            >
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Nelson et al.</strong>: &ldquo;Biosphere
                            2&rsquo;s Lessons about Living on Earth and in
                            Space,&rdquo; <em
                                >Space: Science &amp; Technology</em
                            > (2021). <a
                                href="https://spj.science.org/doi/10.34133/2021/8067539"
                                target="_blank">Full Text</a
                            >
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>NASA CELSS Program</strong>: NASA Conference
                            Publication 2378, &ldquo;Controlled Ecological Life
                            Support System&rdquo; (1985). <a
                                href="https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19930033435"
                                target="_blank">NASA NTRS</a
                            >
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Wheeler et al.</strong>: &ldquo;Crop
                            productivities and radiation use efficiencies for
                            bioregenerative life support,&rdquo; <em
                                >Advances in Space Research</em
                            > (2008).
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>ISS ECLSS</strong>: Environmental Control
                            and Life Support Systems. <a
                                href="https://www.nasa.gov/reference/environmental-control-and-life-support-systems-eclss/"
                                target="_blank">NASA Reference</a
                            >
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                    <h3>Population &amp; Artificial Gravity</h3>
                    <ol start="9">
                        <li>
                            <strong>Smith, Cameron M.</strong>:
                            &ldquo;Estimation of a genetically viable population
                            for multigenerational interstellar voyaging,&rdquo; <em
                                >Acta Astronautica</em
                            > 97 (2014). <a
                                href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0094576513004669"
                                target="_blank">ScienceDirect</a
                            >
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>NASA Technical Report</strong>:
                            &ldquo;Chapter 3: History of Artificial
                            Gravity.&rdquo; <a
                                href="https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/20070001009/downloads/20070001009.pdf"
                                target="_blank">NASA NTRS</a
                            >
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Globus, Al</strong>: &ldquo;Space Settlement
                            Population Rotation Tolerance.&rdquo; <a
                                href="https://space.nss.org/wp-content/uploads/Space-Settlement-Population-Rotation-Tolerance-Globus.pdf"
                                target="_blank">NSS</a
                            >
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                    <h3>Generation Ships</h3>
                    <ol start="12">
                        <li>
                            <strong>Hein, Andreas M. et al.</strong>:
                            &ldquo;World Ships &mdash; Architectures &amp;
                            Feasibility Revisited,&rdquo; <em
                                >Journal of the British Interplanetary Society</em
                            > 65 (2012).
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>T.A. Heppenheimer</strong>: <em
                                >Colonies in Space</em
                            > (1977). <a
                                href="https://space.nss.org/colonies-in-space-chapter-9-up-on-the-farm/"
                                target="_blank"
                                >NSS &mdash; Ch. 9: Up on the Farm</a
                            >
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                    <p class="cite-note">
                        Visualization parameters calibrated to the 1975 NASA
                        Ames/Stanford Summer Study specifications. Population
                        estimates extrapolated from NASA SP-413 baseline of
                        10,000 residents at R=830m, r=65m.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </body>
</html>

